  "identifier": "femr",
  "name": "FEMR",
  "alternateName": [
    "Framework for Electronic Medical Records"
  ],
  "description": "Python framework for large-scale self-supervised learning on electronic health records. Provides tooling for converting raw EHR data to the MEDS (Medical Event Data Standard) format, building code ontologies (SNOMED, LOINC, ICD), and training clinical foundation models — including MOTOR, a BERT-style model pretrained on structured EHR events. Supports labelling functions, feature extraction pipelines, and evaluation utilities. Designed to lower the barrier to reproducing and extending EHR foundation model research. Apache 2.0. From the Shah Lab at Stanford Medicine.",
